IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cr2-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- APPLICATIONS (regulations 42 to 46.1).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Regulations text file, lines 441 to 474.
--
-- Recovery of an overpayment by deduction (42); how an application is made, when a denied disability application
-- is deemed a retirement pension application, and when an application is forwarded to a provincial plan (43);
-- who may apply for an incapable person or for a division after a death (44); withdrawing an application (45);
-- how a person is notified of a division or an assignment (46, 46.1).
--
-- Days are counted in whole days from the day named; "N days after the day on which ..." ends N days after that
-- day, inclusive. A month is counted by the calendar months of the core (cpp-core-calendar.l4).
-- Judgments the text hands to the Minister ("if the Minister is satisfied", "that the Minister deems necessary")
-- are BOOLEAN inputs named for them.

§ `Part V -- Applications (regulations 42 to 46.1)`

§§ `Regulation 42 -- recovery of an overpayment by deduction from a benefit`

-- src:442 | 42 For the purpose of subsection 66(2.1) of the Act, an amount of indebtedness that is owing may be deducted and retained out of the whole or any portion of a benefit that is payable to the person or the person’s estate or succession, under this Act or any other Act or program administered by the Minister, that will recover the overpayment in a single payment or in instalments, in any amount that does not cause undue hardship to the person or the person’s estate or succession.
@ref Reg 42 (src:442)
GIVEN `an overpayment is owing by the person or the person's estate or succession` IS A BOOLEAN   -- the indebtedness of subsection 66(2.1) of the Act; out of range: section 66(2.1) (piece cp4)
      `a benefit is payable to the person or the person's estate or succession under the Act or another Act or program administered by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount to be deducted` IS A NUMBER
      `the benefit payable` IS A NUMBER
      `the overpayment still owing` IS A NUMBER
      `the deduction would cause undue hardship to the person or the person's estate or succession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 42 — an amount owing may be deducted and retained out of a benefit payable`
    `an overpayment is owing by the person or the person's estate or succession`
    `a benefit is payable to the person or the person's estate or succession under the Act or another Act or program administered by the Minister`
    `the amount to be deducted`
    `the benefit payable`
    `the overpayment still owing`
    `the deduction would cause undue hardship to the person or the person's estate or succession` MEANS
    `an overpayment is owing by the person or the person's estate or succession`
        AND `a benefit is payable to the person or the person's estate or succession under the Act or another Act or program administered by the Minister`
        AND `the amount to be deducted` GREATER THAN 0
        AND `the amount to be deducted` AT MOST `the benefit payable`
        AND `the amount to be deducted` AT MOST `the overpayment still owing`
        AND (NOT `the deduction would cause undue hardship to the person or the person's estate or succession`)

§§ `Regulation 43 -- application for a benefit, for a division or for an assignment`

-- src:445 | 43 (1) An application for a benefit, for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1 of the Act or for an assignment of a portion of a retirement pension under section 65.1 of the Act shall be made by submitting it to the Minister in writing.
@ref Reg 43(1) (src:445)
GIVEN `the application is submitted to the Minister in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 43(1) — an application for a benefit, a division or an assignment is made as the Regulations require`
    `the application is submitted to the Minister in writing` MEANS
    `the application is submitted to the Minister in writing`

-- 43(1.1): a denied application for a disability pension is deemed, on request, to be an application for a retirement pension.
-- First limb: the applicant has reached 60 between the time of the application and the time of its denial, 60 being
-- reached on the date section 2(2) of the Act deems (regulation 43 is not among the provisions section 2(2) excepts);
-- second limb: the applicant would have been entitled to a retirement pension had they applied for one then.
-- src:446 | (1.1) Where an application for a disability pension has been denied, and the applicant has reached 60 years of age between the time of the application and the time of its denial or would have been entitled to a retirement pension if he had applied therefor at the time of application for the disability pension, that application shall, on request made by or on behalf of the applicant, be deemed to be an application for a retirement pension if the request is made
@ref Reg 43(1.1) (src:446)
GIVEN `the application for a disability pension has been denied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the date of the application for the disability pension` IS A DATE
      `the date the application was denied` IS A DATE
      `the applicant would have been entitled to a retirement pension if the applicant had applied for it at the time of the application for the disability pension` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 44(1)(a) (piece cp3)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 43(1.1) — a denied application for a disability pension is one that may be deemed an application for a retirement pension`
    `the application for a disability pension has been denied`
    `date of birth`
    `the date of the application for the disability pension`
    `the date the application was denied`
    `the applicant would have been entitled to a retirement pension if the applicant had applied for it at the time of the application for the disability pension` MEANS
    `the application for a disability pension has been denied`
        AND (    (    reached60 AT LEAST `the date of the application for the disability pension`
                  AND reached60 AT MOST `the date the application was denied`)
              OR `the applicant would have been entitled to a retirement pension if the applicant had applied for it at the time of the application for the disability pension`)
    WHERE
        reached60 MEANS `s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `any other provision` `date of birth` 60

-- 43(1.1)(b): within 90 days following the month in which the applicant is notified of the denial or, where the denial
-- is finally confirmed on appeal, within 90 days after the day on which the applicant is notified of the confirmation.
-- "Following the month" is counted from the last day of that month (fork F-43). Where there is a confirmation, its
-- period is the one that applies (fork F-43).
-- src:447 | (a) in writing to the Minister; and
-- src:448 | (b) within 90 days following the month in which the applicant is notified of the denial or, where the denial is finally confirmed on appeal, within 90 days after the day on which the applicant is notified of the confirmation.
@ref Reg 43(1.1)(b) (src:448)
GIVEN `the date the applicant is notified of the denial` IS A DATE
      `the date the applicant is notified that the denial is finally confirmed on appeal` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 43(1.1)(b) — the last day for the request` `the date the applicant is notified of the denial` `the date the applicant is notified that the denial is finally confirmed on appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the applicant is notified that the denial is finally confirmed on appeal`
    WHEN JUST confirmed THEN `the date a time limit ends` confirmed (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 90)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date a time limit ends` (`the month following the month of a date` `the date the applicant is notified of the denial` PLUS (0 MINUS 1)) (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 90)

@ref Reg 43(1.1) (src:446-448)
GIVEN `the application for a disability pension has been denied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the date of the application for the disability pension` IS A DATE
      `the date the application was denied` IS A DATE
      `the applicant would have been entitled to a retirement pension if the applicant had applied for it at the time of the application for the disability pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is made by or on behalf of the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is made in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the request is made` IS A DATE
      `the date the applicant is notified of the denial` IS A DATE
      `the date the applicant is notified that the denial is finally confirmed on appeal` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 43(1.1) — the application for a disability pension is deemed to be an application for a retirement pension`
    `the application for a disability pension has been denied`
    `date of birth`
    `the date of the application for the disability pension`
    `the date the application was denied`
    `the applicant would have been entitled to a retirement pension if the applicant had applied for it at the time of the application for the disability pension`
    `the request is made by or on behalf of the applicant`
    `the request is made in writing to the Minister`
    `the date the request is made`
    `the date the applicant is notified of the denial`
    `the date the applicant is notified that the denial is finally confirmed on appeal` MEANS
    `reg 43(1.1) — a denied application for a disability pension is one that may be deemed an application for a retirement pension`
        `the application for a disability pension has been denied` `date of birth` `the date of the application for the disability pension`
        `the date the application was denied`
        `the applicant would have been entitled to a retirement pension if the applicant had applied for it at the time of the application for the disability pension`
        AND `the request is made by or on behalf of the applicant`
        AND `the request is made in writing to the Minister`
        AND `the date the request is made` AT MOST
            (`reg 43(1.1)(b) — the last day for the request` `the date the applicant is notified of the denial` `the date the applicant is notified that the denial is finally confirmed on appeal`)

-- 43(2): where the whole benefit is deemed payable under a provincial plan (section 80 agreement), or the division can
-- be determined under that plan, the Minister must forward the application, with a statement of the date it was
-- received, to the authority charged under that plan.
-- src:449 | (2) Where by reason of section 80 of the Act and an agreement under that section with a province providing a comprehensive pension plan the whole amount of any benefit payable to an applicant is deemed to be payable under that plan or where the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings can be determined under that plan in accordance with the agreement, the Minister shall, as soon as possible after an application is received, forward the application, together with a statement of the date on which it was received, to the authority charged under that plan with the duty of receiving applications, calculating the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings and paying benefits.
@ref Reg 43(2) (src:449)
GIVEN `by reason of section 80 of the Act and an agreement under it with a province providing a comprehensive pension plan, the whole amount of any benefit payable to the applicant is deemed to be payable under that plan` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 80 (piece cp5)
      `the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings can be determined under that plan in accordance with the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 43(2) — the Minister must forward the application to the authority charged under the provincial plan`
    `by reason of section 80 of the Act and an agreement under it with a province providing a comprehensive pension plan, the whole amount of any benefit payable to the applicant is deemed to be payable under that plan`
    `the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings can be determined under that plan in accordance with the agreement` MEANS
    `by reason of section 80 of the Act and an agreement under it with a province providing a comprehensive pension plan, the whole amount of any benefit payable to the applicant is deemed to be payable under that plan`
        OR `the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings can be determined under that plan in accordance with the agreement`

§§ `Regulation 44 -- who may apply for someone else`

-- src:451 | 44 (1) Where the Minister is satisfied, by such medical certificates or other documentary evidence as is presented to the Minister or as the Minister may require, that a person, by reason of infirmity, illness, insanity or other cause, is incapable of managing the person’s own affairs, an application for a benefit, for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1 of the Act or for an assignment of a portion of a retirement pension under section 65.1 of the Act may be made on that person’s behalf by another person or by an agency if the Minister is satisfied that such other person or agency is authorized by or pursuant to a law of Canada or of a province to manage that person’s affairs or, where it appears to the Minister that there is no other person or agency so authorized, by any other person or agency approved by the Minister.
@ref Reg 44(1) (src:451)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied by medical certificates or other documentary evidence that the person is incapable of managing the person's own affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the other person or agency is authorized by or pursuant to a law of Canada or of a province to manage the person's affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Minister that there is no other person or agency so authorized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person or agency is approved by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 44(1) — an application may be made on behalf of a person incapable of managing their own affairs`
    `the Minister is satisfied by medical certificates or other documentary evidence that the person is incapable of managing the person's own affairs`
    `the Minister is satisfied that the other person or agency is authorized by or pursuant to a law of Canada or of a province to manage the person's affairs`
    `it appears to the Minister that there is no other person or agency so authorized`
    `the other person or agency is approved by the Minister` MEANS
    `the Minister is satisfied by medical certificates or other documentary evidence that the person is incapable of managing the person's own affairs`
        AND (    `the Minister is satisfied that the other person or agency is authorized by or pursuant to a law of Canada or of a province to manage the person's affairs`
              OR (    `it appears to the Minister that there is no other person or agency so authorized`
                  AND `the other person or agency is approved by the Minister`))

-- src:452 | (2) Where either or both spouses, former spouses or former common-law partners are deceased, an application for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) of the Act may be made by the personal representative or by or on behalf of a child of any of those deceased persons.
@ref Reg 44(2) (src:452)
GIVEN `the application is for a division under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `either or both spouses, former spouses or former common-law partners are deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by or on behalf of a child of any of those deceased persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 44(2) — an application for a division may be made after a death`
    `the application is for a division under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) of the Act`
    `either or both spouses, former spouses or former common-law partners are deceased`
    `the application is made by the personal representative`
    `the application is made by or on behalf of a child of any of those deceased persons` MEANS
    `the application is for a division under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) of the Act`
        AND `either or both spouses, former spouses or former common-law partners are deceased`
        AND (`the application is made by the personal representative`
             OR `the application is made by or on behalf of a child of any of those deceased persons`)

§§ `Regulation 45 -- withdrawing an application`

-- src:453 | 45 (1) Where no payment of a benefit has been made in respect of an application for a benefit made after May 28, 1975, the applicant may withdraw the application by sending to the Minister a written notice to that effect at any time before the commencement of payment of the benefit.
-- src:454 | (2) Where an application for a benefit has been withdrawn pursuant to subsection (1), the application shall not thereafter be used for the purpose of determining the applicant’s eligibility for a benefit.
-- src:455 | (3) An applicant for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) of the Act may withdraw the application by sending a notice in writing to the Minister not later than 60 days after the date of receipt by the applicant of notification of the decision respecting the application.
-- src:456 | (4) Where an application for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) of the Act is withdrawn pursuant to subsection (3), the application shall not thereafter be used for the purpose of determining whether the person in respect of whom the application was submitted is eligible for the division.
-- src:457 | (5) Where an application for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) of the Act has been approved and subsequently withdrawn, notice in writing of the withdrawal shall be given by the Minister to the other spouse, former spouse or former common-law partner or to their respective estates, as the case may be.
@ref Reg 45(1) (src:453)
GIVEN `no payment of a benefit has been made in respect of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the application was made` IS A DATE
      `the notice of withdrawal is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is sent to the Minister before the commencement of payment of the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 45(1) — an applicant may withdraw an application for a benefit`
    `no payment of a benefit has been made in respect of the application`
    `the date the application was made`
    `the notice of withdrawal is in writing`
    `the notice is sent to the Minister before the commencement of payment of the benefit` MEANS
    `no payment of a benefit has been made in respect of the application`
        AND `the date the application was made` GREATER THAN (YearMonthDay 1975 5 28)
        AND `the notice of withdrawal is in writing`
        AND `the notice is sent to the Minister before the commencement of payment of the benefit`

@ref Reg 45(2) (src:454)
GIVEN `the application has been withdrawn under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 45(2) — the application may be used afterwards to determine the applicant's eligibility for a benefit`
    `the application has been withdrawn under subsection (1)` MEANS
    (NOT `the application has been withdrawn under subsection (1)`)

@ref Reg 45(3) (src:455)
GIVEN `the date the applicant received notification of the decision respecting the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 45(3) — the last day to withdraw an application for a division`
    `the date the applicant received notification of the decision respecting the application` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` `the date the applicant received notification of the decision respecting the application` (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 60)

@ref Reg 45(3) (src:455)
GIVEN `the application is for a division under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the applicant received notification of the decision respecting the application` IS A DATE
      `the date the notice of withdrawal is sent to the Minister` IS A DATE
      `the notice of withdrawal is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 45(3) — an applicant may withdraw an application for a division`
    `the application is for a division under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) of the Act`
    `the date the applicant received notification of the decision respecting the application`
    `the date the notice of withdrawal is sent to the Minister`
    `the notice of withdrawal is in writing` MEANS
    `the application is for a division under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) of the Act`
        AND `the notice of withdrawal is in writing`
        AND `the date the notice of withdrawal is sent to the Minister` AT LEAST `the date the applicant received notification of the decision respecting the application`
        AND `the date the notice of withdrawal is sent to the Minister` AT MOST
            (`reg 45(3) — the last day to withdraw an application for a division` `the date the applicant received notification of the decision respecting the application`)

@ref Reg 45(4) (src:456)
GIVEN `the application for a division has been withdrawn under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 45(4) — the application may be used afterwards to determine whether the person is eligible for the division`
    `the application for a division has been withdrawn under subsection (3)` MEANS
    (NOT `the application for a division has been withdrawn under subsection (3)`)

@ref Reg 45(5) (src:457)
GIVEN `the application for a division has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application has subsequently been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 45(5) — the Minister must give written notice of the withdrawal to the other spouse, former spouse or former common-law partner or their estates`
    `the application for a division has been approved`
    `the application has subsequently been withdrawn` MEANS
    `the application for a division has been approved` AND `the application has subsequently been withdrawn`

§§ `Regulations 46 and 46.1 -- notifying a division and an assignment`

-- src:458 | 46 (1) A notification required by subsection 55.2(4) of the Act shall be effected by giving notice in writing.
@ref Reg 46(1) (src:458)
GIVEN `the notification is given by notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 46(1) — a notification required by subsection 55.2(4) of the Act is effected as the Regulations require`
    `the notification is given by notice in writing` MEANS
    `the notification is given by notice in writing`

-- 46(2): "such of the following information as is applicable". The text does not say when an item is applicable, so
-- the items that apply are an input (fork F-46); item (g) applies only if the Minister deems the information necessary.
-- src:459 | (2) A notification required by subsection 55(8) or 55.2(10) of the Act shall be effected by giving notice in writing containing such of the following information as is applicable:
-- src:460 | (a) the dates of marriage and dissolution of marriage of the persons subject to the division;
-- src:461 | (b) the period of cohabitation for which the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings has been made;
-- src:462 | (c) the amount of unadjusted pensionable earnings, prior to the division, of the persons subject to the division;
-- src:463 | (d) the amount of unadjusted pensionable earnings of the persons subject to the division as a result of the division;
-- src:464 | (e) the effect of the division on any benefit that is payable to or in respect of the persons subject to the division;
-- src:465 | (f) a statement of the right to make a request for a reconsideration referred to in subsection 81(1) of the Act; and
-- src:466 | (g) any other information that the Minister deems necessary.
@ref Reg 46(2) (src:459-466)
GIVEN `the items that are applicable` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of the notice of a division`
      `the items the notice contains` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of the notice of a division`
GIVETH A LIST OF `cr2 Item of the notice of a division`
`reg 46(2) — the items a notification of a division still lacks` `the items that are applicable` `the items the notice contains` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN item YIELD NOT (elem item `the items the notice contains`)) `the items that are applicable`

@ref Reg 46(2) (src:459-466)
GIVEN `the notification is given by notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the items that are applicable` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of the notice of a division`
      `the items the notice contains` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of the notice of a division`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 46(2) — a notification required by subsection 55(8) or 55.2(10) of the Act is effected as the Regulations require`
    `the notification is given by notice in writing` `the items that are applicable` `the items the notice contains` MEANS
    `the notification is given by notice in writing`
        AND null (`reg 46(2) — the items a notification of a division still lacks` `the items that are applicable` `the items the notice contains`)

-- src:467 | (3) A division referred to in subsection 55.1(5) of the Act may be cancelled pursuant to that subsection within the period of 60 days after the making of the division.
@ref Reg 46(3) (src:467)
GIVEN `the date the division was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 46(3) — the last day to cancel a division under subsection 55.1(5) of the Act` `the date the division was made` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` `the date the division was made` (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 60)

@ref Reg 46(3) (src:467)
GIVEN `the date the division was made` IS A DATE
      `the date of the cancellation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 46(3) — a division may be cancelled under subsection 55.1(5) of the Act` `the date the division was made` `the date of the cancellation` MEANS
    `the date of the cancellation` AT LEAST `the date the division was made`
        AND `the date of the cancellation` AT MOST (`reg 46(3) — the last day to cancel a division under subsection 55.1(5) of the Act` `the date the division was made`)

-- src:468 | 46.1 (1) A notification required by subsection 65.1(5) of the Act shall be effected by giving notice in writing.
-- src:469 | (2) A notification required by subsection 65.1(12) of the Act shall be effected by giving notice in writing containing the following information:
-- src:470 | (a) the month with which the assignment commences in accordance with subsection 65.1(10) of the Act;
-- src:471 | (b) the portion of retirement pension assigned; and
-- src:472 | (c) a statement of the right to make a request for a reconsideration referred to in subsection 81(1) of the Act.
@ref Reg 46.1(1) (src:468)
GIVEN `the notification is given by notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 46.1(1) — a notification required by subsection 65.1(5) of the Act is effected as the Regulations require`
    `the notification is given by notice in writing` MEANS
    `the notification is given by notice in writing`

@ref Reg 46.1(2) (src:469-472)
GIVEN `the notification is given by notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the month with which the assignment commences in accordance with subsection 65.1(10) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the portion of retirement pension assigned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the right to make a request for a reconsideration referred to in subsection 81(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 46.1(2) — a notification required by subsection 65.1(12) of the Act is effected as the Regulations require`
    `the notification is given by notice in writing`
    `the notice states the month with which the assignment commences in accordance with subsection 65.1(10) of the Act`
    `the notice states the portion of retirement pension assigned`
    `the notice states the right to make a request for a reconsideration referred to in subsection 81(1) of the Act` MEANS
    `the notification is given by notice in writing`
        AND `the notice states the month with which the assignment commences in accordance with subsection 65.1(10) of the Act`
        AND `the notice states the portion of retirement pension assigned`
        AND `the notice states the right to make a request for a reconsideration referred to in subsection 81(1) of the Act`
